   "text": {
    "L1": "A book corner is a square corner. We call this a right angle.",
    "L2": "Fold a paper twice to make a square-corner tester, then place it on the corner.",
    "L3": "If the tester fits exactly, the corner is a right angle. The arms can be short or long.",
    "L4": "MYTH: longer arms make a bigger angle. Not true: an angle is how wide the arms open, not their length.",
    "L5": "Turning a shape does not change its angles. A tilted square corner is still a right angle.",
    "L6": "In a circle, every point on the edge is the same distance from the centre.",
    "L7": "Hold one end of a string at the centre and keep it tight while the other end moves around.",
    "L8": "Now check: two square corners with different arm lengths are what size compared with each other?"
   },
